{
  "abstract": "Can a Transformer train without a backward pass—zero pullbacks, VJP helpers, or same-step relays inside `with torch.no_grad():`—while beating matched-subset node perturbation? We study 3-stage delayed Weight Maximization (WM) across 236 backward-free arms (`exp26`–`exp76`, plus 3 compositional, 7 pullback, and 66 BP/surrogate arms; $312$ arms $=935$ runs) on `d6` ($L=6,D\\in\\{256..768\\}$, $360$–$1,004$st) and `50.3M` ($L=8,D=512,T=2,048$, $100$st). We prove stream-partitioned WM & its $\\operatorname{diag}(1-x_i^2/D)$ `RMSNorm` mean (Prop. 1), commute $W_v$ with attention ($+0.9069$ cos, Prop. 2), route `wte` via a diagonal skip (Prop. 3), bound `RMSNorm` residual by $\\kappa_4(x)/D$ (Prop. 4), prove tangent-projection variance drop (Prop. 5), derive the Wiener-MMSE key filter $W_{\\tau,s}^{\\text{MMSE}}(M)$ ($3.22\\times$ cos, Prop. 6), apply Zhang et al.'s [12] groupwise Stiefel polar factor $\\operatorname{St}(g d_h,D)^{H/g}$ (Prop. 7), prove linear `Exact-SVD Taper` $s_r(\\gamma)$ vs. `PrePolar-Blend` (Prop. 8), and prove un-equilibrated cubic Gram tapering $G_3=(G_n G_n^\\top)G_n$ (`Gram3-PrePolar-Blend` & `Exact-SVD Gram3 Taper` $\\gamma_Q=0.20,\\gamma_K=0.35$, Prop. 9) alongside Gavish-Donoho [13] shrinkage $\\eta^*(y)$. Across $D\\in\\{256..768\\}$ ($360$st), `Gram3-PrePolar-Blend` $M=4$ hits **`2.0640, 2.0337, 2.0206, 2.0138` DEV BPB—beating 4-mat BP (`2.0789..2.0433`) and recovering $147.2\\%..159.7\\%$ of shared-LR 6-mat BP (`2.0590..2.0153`)**. At $720$st ($D=384$), 6-mat WM hits **`1.9407\\pm0.0006` (`29.07s`, Gram3-Blend) / `1.9401\\pm0.0021` (`205.88` PPL, Gavish-Donoho)—beating 4-mat BP (`1.9423`) and recovering $112.1\\%/113.3\\%$ of shared-LR 6-mat BP (`1.8904`) and $64.7\\%/65.4\\%$ of Per-Head BP (`1.8518`)**; $840$st $M=2$ hits **`1.9337` (`22.90s`)**. On `50.3M`, WM hits **`1.8620` (`Exact-SVD Taper` $M=2$), `1.8583` (`Gram3-Blend` $M=2$), and `1.8554` (`184.97` PPL, $M=4$)** vs. BP $1.6989$.",
  "author": "cartan_geodesic",
  "change_summary": "1. Proposition 9 & Marchenko-Pastur Bulk Audit (exp76 Part 1, Check 4F): On ClimbMix d6 (beta=d_h/D=64/384=1/6, median mu_1/6=0.9442, bulk edge 1+sqrt(1/6)=1.4082), only 20.4%-32.2% of per-head (W_Q, W_K) singular modes exceed the Marchenko-Pastur bulk edge (Step-120 sigma_med/sigma_max = 0.2098 on W_Q vs. 0.0964 on W_K). Applying Gavish-Donoho [13] optimal singular-value shrinkage eta*(y) = sqrt(((y^2-beta-1)^2-4*beta)_+)/y zeros out the ~75% noise bulk, hitting 2.0337 +- 0.0017 DEV BPB (1.9961 VAL-B, 266.21 PPL, 48.96s) at 360st and 1.9401 +- 0.0021 DEV BPB (1.9051 VAL-B, 205.88 PPL, 98.28s) at 720st—beating 720-step 4-Matrix Exact Global Backpropagation (1.9423 +- 0.0031) at equal tokens. To eliminate SVD overhead and escape the 2-pass equilibration diagonal collapse of PrePolar-Blend on diag(4,2,1,1) -> I_4, we prove (Proposition 9) that forming G_3 = (G_n G_n^T) G_n from un-equilibrated G_n = G_h/||G_h||_F (two 64x64/64x384 matmuls, zero SVD) cubes singular values (suppressing bulk modes sigma_r <= sigma_1/3 by >=27x in amplitude / >=729x in energy) and matches Exact-SVD Gram3 Taper on diag(4,2,1,1) to <1e-15. With tier-asymmetric gamma_Q=0.20, gamma_K=0.35, Gram3-PrePolar-Blend reaches 2.0337 +- 0.0004 in 14.49s at 360st (matching Exact-SVD Gram3 Taper 2.0337 +- 0.0004 in 48.86s at 3.38x lower time), 1.9407 +- 0.0006 in 29.07s at 720st (matching Exact-SVD Gram3 Taper 1.9408 +- 0.0007 in 97.93s and beating 4-Matrix Exact BP 1.9423), and 1.9337 +- 0.0015 (1.8990 VAL-B, 202.29 PPL) in 22.90s at 840st (Upper-Half M=2). 2. Width Scaling Across D in {256, 384, 512, 768} & Double Dissociation on Noise-Free Backpropagation (exp75 Arms 1-6, exp76 Arms 14-20): Across D in {256, 384, 512, 768} at 360st, PrePolar-Blend (gamma_QK=0.20, exp75) hits 2.0675, 2.0382, 2.0259, 2.0207 and Gram3-PrePolar-Blend (gamma_Q=0.20, gamma_K=0.35, exp76) hits 2.0640 +- 0.0007, 2.0337 +- 0.0004, 2.0206 +- 0.0013, and 2.0138 +- 0.0002 DEV BPB (where D=768 beats shared-LR 6-Matrix Exact BP 2.0153 by -0.0015 BPB). Crucially, whereas linear PrePolar-Blend slightly improves 360/720st Global BP (1.9899->1.9879; 1.8530->1.8518) and Sub-Block-Skip BP (2.0052->2.0039; 1.8920->1.8904), cubic Gram3-PrePolar-Blend degrades noise-free Global BP (1.9899->1.9929 at 360st; 1.8530->1.8559 at 720st) and Sub-Block-Skip BP (2.0052->2.0071 at 360st; 1.8920->1.8941 at 720st) while improving noisy Delayed WM by -0.0106 and -0.0141 BPB. 3. Native 50.3M Exact-SVD Deconfounding & Cubic Gram Transfer (exp75 Arms 7-8, exp76 Arms 21-22): On 8-layer T=2,048 Native 50.3M Upper-Half (4..7) M=2, un-equilibrated Exact-SVD Polar (gamma=0) scores 1.8747 +- 0.0005 and un-equilibrated Exact-SVD Taper (gamma_QK=0.20) improves by -0.0127 BPB to 1.8620 +- 0.0027 (1.8479 VAL-B, 188.47 PPL), while Gram3-PrePolar-Blend reaches 1.8583 +- 0.0030 (1.8442 VAL-B, 186.53 PPL, 6.04s/step) at M=2 and 1.8595 +- 0.0049 at M=4 (vs. linear PrePolar-Blend 1.8554 +- 0.0008 at M=4).",
